xt-main","children":"How the destination alarm works"}],["$","p",null,{"children":"The alarm is tied to the final station on the tracked train's journey timeline. Once enabled, Trayago monitors the journey's progress using the same running information shown on this page and alerts you as the train nears that station — early enough to gather luggage and get ready, rather than at the moment of arrival. Keep the tab open for the alarm to stay active, and toggle it off at any time."}],["$","p",null,{"children":"Because it works from reported running information, alarm timing is guidance rather than a precise guarantee. A train's delay can change while it is en route."}]]}],["$","div",null,{"className":"space-y-3","children":[["$","h3",null,{"className":"text-base font-bold text-main","children":"Why a train destination alarm is useful"}],["$","p",null,{"children":"Overnight journeys are the obvious case — falling asleep and waking past your station is a common and expensive mistake. It also helps on long-distance routes where arrival drifts by hours, at unfamiliar stations where you cannot recognise the platform, and on early-morning arrivals when nobody in the coach is awake to ask. Mostly it removes the need to keep checking the phone, which is the whole point of tracking a journey."}]]}],["$","div",null,{"className":"space-y-4","children":[["$","h2",null,{"className":"text-xl font-black text-main","children":"Train tracker — frequently asked questions"}],["$","dl",null,{"className":"space-y-5","children":[["$","div","What is a train tracker?",{"className":"space-y-1.5","children":[["$","dt",null,{"className":"text-sm font-bold text-main","children":"What is a train tracker?"}],["$","dd",null,{"className":"text-sm text-secondary leading-relaxed","children":"A train tracker follows a train's progress along its route on a given day. You enter the train number and it shows where the train has been reported, which station is next, how it is running against the timetable, and the station-by-station journey ahead."}]]}],"$L4b","$L4c","$L4d","$L4e","$L4f"]}]]}],"$L50"]}]}]
